nize datasets stored in databases, and secondly, to expose you to different kinds of business datasets and potential uses. In other words, this is a unique SQL course targeted at business students. \u00a0", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GM", "acadGroup": "BU", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2769, "crseId": 367646, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "NBAY", "catalogNbr": "6560", "titleShort": "Valuations", "titleLong": "Valuations", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 14328, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "12:00PM", "timeEnd": "01:50PM", "startDt": "10/26/2020", "endDt": "12/07/2020", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 6, "netid": "eab348", "firstName": "Elizabeth", "middleName": "Anne", "lastName": "Berger"}], "pattern": "MW", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Taught in NYC at Cornell Tech. Enrollment limited to: Cornell Tech students. Please note: non-MBA Students must take TECH 5310 - Business Fundamentals as a prerequisite.\nDrop Deadline: Friday, October 30th  4:00pm"}], "campus": "NYT", "campusDescr": "New York Tech Campus", "location": "NYCTECH", "locationDescr": "Cornell Tech", "startDt": "10/21/2020", "endDt": "12/08/2020", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "OL", "instrModeDescrshort": "OL", "instrModeDescr": "Online", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 1.5, "unitsMaximum": 1.5, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "7W2", "sessionBeginDt": "10/21/2020", "sessionEndDt": "12/21/2020", "sessionLong": "Seven Week - Second", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "This course provides fundamental concepts and tools to value assets, including firms and projects, using an economic framework. It begins with an overview of two approaches to valuation: 1) discounted cash flow (DCF) and 2) valuation by multiples using comparable assets. We will first discuss the fact that valuation by multiples and the DCF approach are one and the same. Then, we will discuss the DCF approaches in detail, including projections and costs of capital. We will wrap up the course with a case discussion of valuing \"hyper-growth\" technology firms and issues specific to valuing high-tech/start-up firms. This course is especially useful to anyone preparing for a career role in product management, including marketing and operations, and valuing entrepreneurial opportunities (e.g., startups). Both conceptual understanding and practical implementations through case studies will be emphasized.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: TECH 5310.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: Cornell Tech students.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GM", "acadGroup": "BU", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCri